# AIDE environment variables — example only. Copy to .env and fill in.
# .env is gitignored. Never commit a populated .env.
#
# Sovereign-compute doctrine: do NOT add cloud LLM API keys here. AIDE's
# cognition stays local. The variables below are for transport tokens
# only (Telegram bots that relay to the local chassis).

# Cipher bot (existing) — long-polling Telegram bot for AIDE remote
# control. The chassis's telegram service reads this on startup and
# connects to Telegram's getUpdates endpoint. Per P5 the chassis never
# kills a foreign llama-server or python.exe — but the token here
# points at a Telegram account the operator controls.
AIDE_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=

# DC_AIDEbot (forthcoming) — public Telegram bot that relays user
# messages to the local Cipher-as-desktop-control flow. Per
# docs/evidence/aide-p6-desktop-control the bot runs in the SAME
# process as the chassis (single source of desktop truth). Long-polling,
# same transport. The token goes ONLY into your local .env file —
# never in chat, never in a commit, never in a screenshot.
AIDE_TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN_DC_AIDE=

# Optional: Telegram chat_id allowlist (comma-separated). When set,
# the bots reject any incoming message whose from.id is NOT in this
# list. Strongly recommended for the public bot (DC_AIDEbot) to
# prevent arbitrary strangers from driving your AIDE.
# AIDE_TELEGRAM_ALLOWED_CHAT_IDS=123456789,987654321
